@* A native <dialog>. showModal() gives the focus trap, the inert background,
   Escape and the top layer — the parts Radix spends most of its bytes on.

   When the content comes from the SERVER, prefer an Unpoly overlay instead: up-layer="new"
   renders a real, bookmarkable route into a modal. <Dialog> is for content the page already has. *@
<DialogTrigger Target="demo-dialog" Variant="outline">Edit profile</DialogTrigger>

<Dialog Id="demo-dialog">
    <DialogHeader>
        <DialogTitle>Edit profile</DialogTitle>
        <DialogDescription>Changes are saved when you submit.</DialogDescription>
    </DialogHeader>

    <FormField For="name" Label="Name">
        <Input id="name" name="name" value="Marta Ruiz" />
    </FormField>

    <DialogFooter>
        <DialogClose>Cancel</DialogClose>
        <Button>Save</Button>
    </DialogFooter>
</Dialog>
